===Level 82–99: Pickpocketing vyres===
Pickpocketing [[vyre]]s at level 82 with rogue equipment, dodgy necklaces, and the [[Ardougne Diary#Hard|hard Ardougne Diary]] completed will get 120,000–180,000 experience per hour and profit {{Mmgprofit|Pickpocketing vyres}} coins per hour, depending on Thieving level. This will require completion of the [[Sins of the Father]].

As an alternative to using food, players may opt to use [[prayer regeneration potion]]s in conjunction with the [[Redemption]] prayer. As the vyres inflict a flat 5 health points worth of damage, the prayer should be activated by at least 6 health points.

===Level 85–99: Pickpocketing elves===
Pickpocketing [[Elf (Thieving)|elves]] in [[Prifddinas]] is a slower but profitable alternative after completing [[Song of the Elves]]. The elves in Prifddinas yield [[enhanced crystal teleport seed]]s which can be sold for high profit. 

At level 99 players can gain around 150,000 experience per hour and {{Mmgprofit|Pickpocketing elves}} coins per hour assuming that players use [[dodgy necklace]]s, and full [[rogue equipment]].

===Level 20–99: Stealing from Port Roberts stalls===
 
With 50 [[Sailing]], players can steal from the stalls in [[Port Roberts]]. Unlike regular stalls, these stalls do not deplete when players steal from them, and as such will be stolen from repeatedly when clicked once. At the same time, [[Market Guard (Port Roberts)|market guards]] patrol with set timings and will send the player to jail if the player steals from a stall which a guard is looking at. 

The goal is to steal 4 times from the primary stall (the highest level stall available) and 2 times from the secondary stall (the second-highest level stall available) in a set cycle.

The setup to move in sync with the guards is as follows:
# Find your primary and secondary stall.
# Locate the tile near the primary stall that the guards stand on when they are guarding the primary stall.
# Stand on that exact tile, and wait for a guard to go onto it.
# The guard will disappear under you. As soon as you see them again (as they leave the tile), click the primary stall.
# Steal 4 times from the primary stall, and then click the secondary stall.
# Steal 2 times from the secondary stall, and then click the primary stall again. From this point on, you should never have to worry about the guards. The 4-2 pattern will be in sync with the guards without major mistakes.

If you make a mistake and fear the guards may catch you, wait on the primary stall tile and repeat from step 4 again. If arrested, pick the lock to the jail cell ([[lockpick]] not required) or bribe the [[Jail Guard (Port Roberts)|guard]] with 500 coins. Alternatively, you can use the [[Sailors' amulet]] to teleport right back near the stalls.

There is a [[Bank Deposit Box]] directly north of the market for banking your goods. You may also use storage items like the [[Fish barrel]], [[Gem bag]], or [[Coal bag]] for longer trips between deposits, or using [[Superheat Item]] to combine ores without losing ticks. 

Experience rates shown in the table below assume no mistakes. With some practice, it is possible to consistently get the listed rates.

